  "properties": {
    "title": "GRID3 NGA - Operational Wards v4.0",
    "description": "The GRID3 NGA – Operational Wards v4.0 dataset provides operational ward boundary polygons for all 36 states and the Federal Capital Territory (FCT). This release updates the boundaries for 31 states and the FCT. Benue, Cross River, Ebonyi, Plateau and Taraba are included but have not been updated, and will be updated in the December release. This version supersedes the previously published Version 3.0 (https://doi.org/10.7916/2pfj-hq78). The following changes were made: v4.0 includes major updates for Akwa Ibom, Anambra, Edo, Ekiti, Imo, Lagos, Ondo, and Rivers states (which had not been updated since v1.0) and supersedes v3.0 for the remaining 24 states, which have minor edits Ward boundaries were aligned to Small Settlement Areas (SSA) and Built-Up Areas (BUA) type settlement extents for all states and FCT State boundaries were aligned to SSA and BUA type settlement extents for all states and FCT, Abuja Ward boundaries were aligned to blocks for all states and FCT Ward boundaries modified based on PoI datasets (MLoS and health facility) and the boundaries aligned to major roads and water bodies (rivers and lakes for Akwa Ibom, Anambra, Edo, Ekiti, Imo, Lagos, Ondo, and Rivers) Kano Ward boundaries were modified based on National Malaria Elimination Programme (NMEP) 2022 and 2025 version datasets Known issues identified after publication: Ikuru ward geometry in Andoni LGA, Rivers State, was removed in error, and small gaps may occur along the borders of the five states not updated in this release; both will be corrected in our next release (see Table 2a, Notes by states and Known Data Limitations). Keywords: Boundaries",
    "license": "The data and accompanying document are licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International, CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0) and specified in legal code (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode)",
